    { name: "Clogging at high speeds", cause: "Hotend heat creep — the melt zone extends too far up into the cold zone, causing soft filament to jam.", fix: "Ensure part cooling fan is running at full speed. Check that the heatsink fan is working. Consider a high-flow hotend (Rapido 2, Dragon HF) for sustained high-speed printing." },
